course: dictionary
lesson: 2605
title: A depot is where things are kept
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A depot is a large building or yard where things are kept until they are needed. Read the words around depot to find its meaning. «Electric buses charge at the depot overnight or quickly at some stops.» Charge and overnight are the clues: the buses stay somewhere at night, so a depot must be a place where buses are kept.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Electric buses charge at the place where they are kept overnight» still makes sense, so your meaning fits. You can use the same check with any new word.
explain: The word can also be used for other things. A fuel depot keeps fuel, a supply depot keeps supplies, and a delivery depot keeps parcels before they go out. In maths, «trucks leave the depot» tells you the depot is where the trucks start their journey.
fact: A depot is a large building or yard where goods, vehicles or supplies are kept until they are needed.
fact: A bus depot is a place where buses are parked, cleaned and repaired.
fact: In the US, a depot can mean a small railway or bus station.
fact: Phrases you may meet: fuel depot, supply depot, delivery depot, return to the depot.
fact: In a story, a depot is often a busy place full of lorries or trains.
exercise: «Electric buses charge at the depot overnight.» Where do the buses charge? | A bus station for passengers only | *At the depot, where they are kept | In a shop window | On the school playground
exercise: «Trucks leave the depot at dawn.» What is the depot in this sentence? | *The place the trucks start from | A hospital | A river | A kind of road
exercise: Which phrase means a place where parcels wait before they are sent out? | Rainy day | Bus shelter | Dinner queue | *Delivery depot
test: «The council keeps salt and grit at the depot for icy roads.» What is the depot used for? | *Keeping supplies until they are needed | A swimming pool | Parking cars for a school trip | Selling ice cream
test: What does a bus depot do with the buses? | Paints them blue for the summer | *Parks, cleans and repairs them | Uses them as classrooms | Sells them to passengers
exam: «Electric buses charge at the depot overnight.» Which clue helps you most to work out what depot means? | Charge, because phones charge too | *Overnight, because the buses stay somewhere at night | Buses, because a bus is always a school bus | Electric, because only electric things have depots
